    "narrative": "The Austin Waves enter today\u2019s slate with **Gunnar Henderson** headlining our roster as the premier play. His 81.88 efficiency score is anchored by a favorable matchup against Ober (xERA 4.78) and a significant boost from his leadoff spot, but the critical factor is his stolen base potential; with a slow-to-the-plate pitcher on the mound, **Gunnar Henderson** is primed to exploit the basepaths, a high-value outcome for our team's structural needs. **Luis Robert Jr.** (77.40) and **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.** (74.45) follow closely behind as our most reliable sources of power, both benefiting from dynamic platoon advantages against left-handed starters. **Kyle Tucker** (74.02) remains an auto-start despite facing Wacha, as his elite base projection survives even middling matchups, ensuring our core lineup maintains a high floor across the counting categories.\n\nThe most difficult roster decision today was excluding **Nasim Nunez**, who finished just shy of the starting lineup with a 46.31 efficiency rating. While his elite speed makes him a weapon, the matchup against Imanaga\u2019s 3.75 xERA suppresses his immediate ceiling, making him the odd man out in favor of higher-projected options like **Sam Antonacci** or **Heliot Ramos**. We are monitoring the lineup status of several players to ensure these 50-range projected scores hold steady; should any late scratches occur, the bench remains thin, especially with **Jordan Westburg** still sidelined on the IL. We are proceeding with caution regarding **Sam Antonacci** and **Heliot Ramos**, whose sub-50 scores represent our current risk threshold; if they see their batting order position drop further, they will be the first to be subbed out to protect our game caps.",
